ollapse\nIf prompted discuss chest pain, travel, OCP\n\nSim Nurse\nAsk for early differential diagnosis \nPrompt learner to consider analgesia","sourceTrigger":"structured A-E completed, time elapsed","transition":null,"actions":[{"id":"pe-1-0","text":"Introduce self and confirm patient identity","objective":"assessment","response":null},{"id":"pe-1-1","text":"Succinct history taking","objective":"assessment","response":null},{"id":"pe-1-2","text":"A-E Assessment","objective":"assessment","response":null},{"id":"pe-1-3","text":"Oxygen therapy","objective":"assessment","response":null}]},{"id":"2","name":"Differential Diagnosis/Investigations","observations":{"rr":24,"spo2":90,"hr":122,"sbp":110,"dbp":70,"temp":37.2},"oxygen":"Room air","rhythm":null,"findings":"Swollen, hot and red left leg. Mildly breathless.","cues":"Sim LeaderPatient to complain of discomfort\nIncreasing hypoxia/tachycardia\n\nSim Nurse\nProvide CXR when asked\nProvide ECG when asked\nProvide ABG when asked\nPrompt learner with patient discomfort\nPrompt learner for anti-emetic if sick\nAsk for most likely diagnosis/differential","sourceTrigger":"Investigations complete/interpretation performed, differential given, time elapsed","transition":null,"actions":[{"id":"pe-2-0","text":"Interpretation of ABG","objective":"interpretation","response":null},{"id":"pe-2-1","text":"Interpretation of ECG","objective":"interpretation","response":null},{"id":"pe-2-2","text":"Interpretation of CXR","objective":"interpretation","response":null},{"id":"pe-2-3","text":"Differential diagnosis that includes PE","objective":"interpretation","response":null},{"id":"pe-2-4","text":"Prescribe analgesia/anti-emetic","objective":"interpretation","response":null}]},{"id":"3","name":"Patient Deterioration/Escalation","observations":{"rr":32,"spo2":86,"hr":135,"sbp":85,"dbp":55,"temp":37.2},"oxygen":"Room air","rhythm":null,"findings":"Swollen, hot and red left leg.  Patient clammy and generally unwell.  Visibly breathless.",